{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Language interoperability","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"anchor":"Language-interoperability"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"bitfields and unnamed fields.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift imports any C structure declared in a C header as a Swift structure. The imported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift structure contains a stored property for each C structure field and an initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose parameters correspond to the stored properties."}]},{"text":"Structures with Default Values","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Structures-with-Default-Values"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If all imported members have default values, Swift also provides a default initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that takes no arguments. For example, given the following C structure:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"occ","code":["struct Color {","    float r, g, b;","};","typedef struct Color Color;"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you import the Color structure, the Swift version is equivalent to the following:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct Color {","    var r: Float","    var g: Float","    var b: Float","","    init()","    init(r: Float, g: Float, b: Float)","}"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Unions","anchor":"Unions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift imports C unions as Swift structures. Although Swift doesn’t support natively"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"declared unions, a C union imported as a Swift structure still behaves like a C union."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, consider a C union named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SchroedingersCat"},{"type":"text","text":" that has an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isAlive"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDead"},{"type":"text","text":" field:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["union SchroedingersCat {","    bool isAlive;","    bool isDead;","};"],"syntax":"occ"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Swift, it’s imported like this:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SchroedingersCat {","    var isAlive: Bool { get set }","    var isDead: Bool { get set }","","    init(isAlive: Bool)","    init(isDead: Bool)","","    init()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because unions in C use the same base memory address for all of their fields, all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the computed properties in a union imported by Swift use the same underlying memory.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"As a result, changing the value of a property on an instance of the imported structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes the value of all other properties defined by that structure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the example below, changing the value of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isAlive"},{"type":"text","text":" computed property on an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SchroedingersCat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure also changes the value of the instance’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDead"},{"type":"text","text":" computed property:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var mittens = SchroedingersCat(isAlive: false)","","print(mittens.isAlive, mittens.isDead)","\/\/ Prints \"false false\"","","mittens.isAlive = true","print(mittens.isDead)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"text":"Bit Fields","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Bit-Fields"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift imports bit fields that are declared in structures, like those found in Foundation’s","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSDecimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, as computed properties. When accessing a computed property corresponding","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to a bit field, Swift automatically converts the value to and from compatible Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"types."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Unnamed Structure and Union Fields","anchor":"Unnamed-Structure-and-Union-Fields"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C "},{"code":"struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"union","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types can define fields that have no name or that are of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unnamed type. Unnamed fields consist of a nested ","type":"text"},{"code":"struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"union","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type with named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, consider a C structure named ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cake","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that contains the fields ","type":"text"},{"code":"layers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"height","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nested within an unnamed union type, and a field ","type":"text"},{"code":"toppings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of an unnamed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"struct type:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Cake {","    union {","        int layers;","        double height;","    };","","    struct {","        bool icing;","        bool sprinkles;","    } toppings;","};"],"syntax":"occ","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cake","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure has been imported, you can use the default initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to create an instance and use it as follows:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var simpleCake = Cake()","simpleCake.layers = 5","print(simpleCake.toppings.icing)","\/\/ Prints \"false\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The imported "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure and its nested types are imported with a memberwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initializer that you can use to initialize the structure with custom values for its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let cake = Cake(","    .init(layers: 2),","    toppings: .init(icing: true, sprinkles: false)",")","","print(\"The cake has \\(cake.layers) layers.\")","\/\/ Prints \"The cake has 2 layers.\"","print(\"Does it have sprinkles?\", cake.toppings.sprinkles ? \"Yes.\" : \"No.\")","\/\/ Prints \"Does it have sprinkles? No.\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the first field of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure is unnamed, its initializer’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter doesn’t have a label. Because the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cake"},{"type":"text","text":" structure has fields with unnamed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types, you use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".init"},{"type":"text","text":" initializers (allowed due to Swift’s type inference) to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set the initial value for each of the structure’s unnamed fields."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift","type":"topic","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the essential types provided by Swift’s standard library."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift"},"d